{"id": "EUVD-2015-9432", "enisaUuid": "b8d69e9b-38e2-3d22-b199-c2218486faa6", "description": "FooSun DotNetCMS 1.0 and 2.0 contains an SQL injection vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to manipulate MSSQL queries through the CityId parameter. Attackers can send GET requests to /user/City_ajax.aspx with UNION SELECT payloads in CityId, concatenated unsanitized into the sys_City query, to extract database information. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-14.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T20:31:26", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.cnblogs.com/rebeyond/p/4951418.html", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/other/dotnetcms-sqli.yaml", "https://web.archive.org/web/20150203014116/http://www.foosun.net/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/foosun-dotnetcms-1.0-2.0-sql-injection-via-city-ajax-aspx"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8cq3-m8mg-6c2h", "CVE-2015-20128"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8788fa6a-3303-3b64-9776-1a01909d27ac", "product": {"name": "DotNetCMS", "vendor": {"name": "FooSun"}}, "product_version": "1.0"}, {"id": "fdbf8eac-d975-3a22-bff0-19cf220131b9", "product": {"name": "DotNetCMS", "vendor": {"name": "FooSun"}}, "product_version": "2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4ab6b47c-aeac-33f5-8dfc-76ae9cb966d3", "vendor": {"name": "FooSun"}}], "isExploited": false}